.SH "NAME"
galaxy\-environments \- list the named environments this API declares
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B galaxy environments
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Prints every environment \-\-environment accepts, with the base URL it selects and which one is used by default. The list comes from the same table galaxy resolves the flag against, so it always describes this version's environments.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, pretty, raw, toon, yaml. Without one, or with auto or pretty, the list is drawn for a reader: the default marked, each base URL behind its name, and colour only when standard output is a terminal. Name a machine format to parse it.
.SH "ENVIRONMENTS"
\-\-environment selects one of these base URLs, or SCALAR_ENVIRONMENT when the flag is not passed, and production is used when neither is. Run galaxy environments to print the same list.
.TP
\fBproduction\fR
https://galaxy.scalar.com (default)
.TP
\fBvoid\fR
https://void.scalar.com/
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Print the environments, then call an endpoint against one of them:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
galaxy environments
galaxy environments \-\-format json
galaxy \-\-environment production COMMAND
.fi
.RE
